# Known-failing suites, as a count, for tools/run_tests.sh.
#
# The suite has a long tail of red. It is red for three different reasons and
# none of them is "the mod is broken":
#
#   ~61 skipped   astra_* A/B harnesses and palettes_gbc, which need a
#                 generated Yellow dataset this repository does not carry
#   ~9 fixed      suites that loaded a module with loadfile and a hand-kept
#                 sibling list; all revived on 2026-09-29 via tests/modload.lua
#   ~6 real       unimplemented features (water_effect_precision's two-form
#                 shader fallback has never existed) or stale expectations
#
# The first push of the Tests workflow went red on exactly this set, which told
# us the workflow's contract was wrong rather than that the suite had regressed:
# a suite with a known tail must gate on that tail not shrinking, not on zero.
# Asserting a ceiling means a NEW failure still fails the run.
#
# 2026-09-29: 38 -> 11, and every step was a FIXTURE or a stale expectation
# rather than a defect in the mod.
#
#   38 -> 32  nine suites loaded a mod module with loadfile and a hand-kept
#             list of sibling names (or answered an unlisted one with `{}`), and
#             every list was out of date. tests/modload.lua resolves siblings
#             off disk the way the installed loader does, so they cannot drift
#             again: voxel_visual_object_filter (3388 checks),
#             battle_scene_visual_sidecar, ram_precache_setting,
#             cut_mesh_refresh, grass_east_edge, city_ground_option,
#             gen3_escalator_camera, atmosphere_camera_projection,
#             building_canopy_regression.
#   32 -> 11  twenty-one more turned out to need the ENGINE's tests.modkit,
#             which lives in the engine checkout and is not in this repository,
#             so standalone they cannot run at all. The runner now reports those
#             as SKIP rather than counting them as failures -- they were never
#             broken, they were being measured by a harness that was not there.
#             With an engine root they run, and that is the number that matters
#             for this codebase's coverage.
#
# The 11 below all run without the engine and all still fail. Each has a
# distinct cause, listed in PROJECT_HANDOFF.md.
#
#   38 -> 35 -> 32 -> 11

11
